Accepted deviation. The second line is USFM 2's figure with every field
empty, `\fig |||||| \fig*`, which the parser reads the way this reference
does — an empty `<figure>` — and reports as `usfm2-figure` (a Warning, so the
case is compared rather than decided on an error). What is left is the first
line's `\fig  | src="figure.png"\fig*`: Paratext keeps the second of the two
spaces after `\fig` as the caption, where whitespace rule 6 on `Text`
(`usfm_ast`) makes all leading whitespace after a marker the marker's, as it
does for `\w  word\w*` and every other marker.

